@* A text line rather than skeleton rows: Songs reads from an in-memory cache and the other pages
   make a single EF call against a local database, so a skeleton would be visible for milliseconds
   and read as flicker.

   The delayed-appear class keeps it invisible for the first 400ms. If the data arrives before then
   the element is gone before the animation starts and nothing ever flashed. The delay lives in CSS
   on purpose — a C# timer would have to make the round trip over SignalR to fire. *@

<div class="px-5 py-4 text-neutral-400 text-sm delayed-appear @Class">
    @(Message ?? L["Common.Loading"].Value)
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Message { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
